      "explanation": "The denominator \\(3\\) in the exponent tells us to use the real cube root. Since \\((-1/5)^3=-1/125\\), and a negative exponent means taking a reciprocal,\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac1{125}\\right)^{-2/3}\n=\\left(-\\frac15\\right)^{-2}\n=\\frac{1}{(-1/5)^2}\n=\\boxed{25}.\n\\]\nThe base is nonzero, so the reciprocal is defined. The answer is \\(25\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
      "id": "cube-root-then-reciprocal",
